OMKUK wrote:
>
> The only altar I've found above DL11 is cross-aligned (Minetown).
> Question is, what's the best way to off the cross-aligned priest?

The best way is strong enough pets to do it for you.  There is often
a polymorph trap somewhere in the mines.

But barring that, do it yourself from a distance.  Use a pickaxe
to remove one of the walls of the shrine.  Put missiles in all of
the open spaces.  Daggers, wands, rocks, whatever.  Then stay out
of reach of the priest but within throwing range.  Do a shooting
contest.  Zap and throw and shot and zap and throw and shoot with
the priest out of range until he dies.  Priests are tough so have
lots of ammunition available.  Every throwable weapon you've
collected in the mines and a couple hundred rocks.  Be very sure
you have far more than enough because if you have to lug more
ammunition, the priest will be fully recovered by the time you
restock.  Sure it will hurt your luck, delete your telepathy,
delete any devine protection and hurt your alignment.  All but
the devine protection can be recovered at the altar with a
bunch of sacraficing and for that matter if you stay long enough
to consider an extinctionist game even the devine protection can
be recovered.  It's not Lawfull behavior but if you *really*
need an altar and the priest is in the way ...

